From 4f1059226c91a74d9f7ef3f80c6921a2fad4fb62 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 12:27:16 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Archipelago sections (Nares, Jones, Lancaster) for the 15 km
 Sep-Oct 2005 run, offline and against GLORYS

config_sep2005_15km_nz50_caa.toml is the production config with three
sections through the Canadian Arctic Archipelago, which together carry the
throughflow that feeds Davis Strait (weak in the model during October). Same
experiment name, so analysis/transports.jl computes them offline from the
existing daily output and analysis/glorys_transports.jl adds them to GLORYS's
reference.

analysis/section_comparison.jl compares every section, offline against
GLORYS (calendar-month means and daily series, with the Archipelago total),
and lists the online transports beside the offline ones where the run has
them, to show the error of the offline method (no daily covariance).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Abhhvm7xByUXxouq5u8r5W
